   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 16,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub director · video\n\n1. **Queue** (Ctrl Enter): the scene and the director come up and everything after the director waits\n   (director flow: hold until apply - no LTX run on an empty composition).\n2. **open director** and build the clip:\n   - **+ layer → light** (Shift L): a night HDRI and lamps; drag the lamp dots on the facade\n   - **● record** (Shift K) in the timeline, move the playhead, move / dim the lamps: keyframes\n   - **♪ audio** (or drop an mp3): waveform, beats and bars; **M** sets markers, keys snap to beats\n   - a paint or image layer over the arcade → **animate (ltx)** on, a video prompt, from / to (s)\n3. **apply**: the workflow runs on - **director sequence** (3b) renders every frame (at its\n   sequence_scale), LTX animates the marked layers inside those frames, Create Video adds the sound.\n   The still-only parts (plan, regions) never wait for the sequence; bypass 3b when you only need the still.\n   3b can also write a delivery file (export: ProRes / PNG / H.264 …).\n\nOn a 12 GB GPU: stage 1 at 0.15-0.2 MP, stage 2 capped at 0.6 MP (stage2_max_mp); a 4 s\nclip with a moving lamp + an animated arcade took ~3.5 min. Laptops: run on mains power.\nSet the path of your scene file on node 1 (.fbx / .blend / .glb / .usd).\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
 ],
